{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued several corrections to articles published on August 25th. These corrections address inaccuracies regarding various topics, ranging from legal matters to personal details about individuals and historical events. The corrections aim to ensure the accuracy and reliability of the information presented to readers. The paper has taken responsibility for these errors and is providing clarifications to ensure the public has access to correct information.\n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction concerns a news article about a new pet theft law. The article incorrectly stated the law applied to \"the UK\" when it actually applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland. Another correction relates to an interview with Juliet Stevenson, where the reporter misidentified the director of her recent project. Additionally, details about the family in the film \"Bend It Like Beckham\" were inaccurate, as they are Sikh, not Muslim.\n\nSection 3\nFurther corrections involve reporting on Venetia Stanley's relationship with Herbert Asquith. The article mistakenly attributed the conversion to Islam to her father, when it was actually her uncle who converted. The paper also clarified the role of Eileen Burbidge, correcting a description of her position at Fertifa. These corrections underscore the importance of meticulous fact-checking in journalism.\n\nSection 4\nThe Guardian encourages readers to report any further errors they may find. Contact information for the Readers’ Editor is provided, including a postal address, email address, and telephone number. The paper is committed to transparency and strives to maintain the highest standards of journalistic integrity.\n\n* The pet theft law applies only to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK.\n* Juliet Stevenson's interview mentioned Alex Lawther, not \"Lowther.\"\n\nP.P.S. The corrections highlight the ongoing effort required to maintain accuracy in news reporting and the importance of reader feedback in identifying and rectifying errors.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00029523781267926097}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.4289199113845825}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.06208682432770729}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.004742208402603865}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.6069830656051636}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.025556569918990135}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.034719809889793396}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -2.307515859603882}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.21311667561531067}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.04903906583786011}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -0.7198897004127502}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -6.6756979322235566e-06}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.0006194579764269292}, {"token": "▁August", "logprob": -6.437094270950183e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -2.145764938177308e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.012905174866318703}, {"token": "▁These", "logprob": -0.007431955076754093}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.10654153674840927}, {"token": "▁address", "logprob": -0.12018901109695435}, {"token": "▁inaccuracies", "logprob": -0.34054240584373474}, {"token": "▁regarding", "logprob": -1.6132726669311523}, {"token": "▁various", "logprob": -0.3967534601688385}, {"token": "▁topics", "logprob": -0.0042130290530622005}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.036470960825681686}, {"token": "▁ranging", "logprob": -0.5569887757301331}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁legal", "logprob": -0.6514554023742676}, {"token": "▁matters", "logprob": -0.12087662518024445}, {"t